    reject toolz.functoolz.curry.func: func is a lambda of the signature registry, not the property of a curry
    note: func is the lambda of a registry entry (expand_sig keeps it as the second item); check_valid runs for every entry of a registered callable that reaches is_valid_args through _check_sigspec: on PyPy every registered key does (the PyPy _check_sigspec, functoolz.py:942), on CPython a key without a signature. The callables come from the client (is_valid_args is public; its docstring names builtins, and the tests pass map, dict, int, sorted, max, bytearray) and from curry._should_curry (the curried builtins, operator functions and excepts). So every lambda that the registry holds on an admitted runtime is a callee, the six package-object keys (curry, flip, juxt, memoize, Compose, InstanceProperty) included: is_valid_args and is_partial_args form one documented introspection role (J4, ruled by b8-ruling-toolz-1, referee, adopted by the lead, 2026-11-24): 193 lambdas; the 97 excluded below are 51 unavailable names and 46 overwritten entries
